{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAG8WeH5FQY5V2CuxScm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` so it now works when only the headers have been written. It still fails once any body data has been written. Before, it checked `w.Written()`, which is also true after headers alone. That meant a `WriteHeaderNow()` before hijacking, which some websocket libraries do, made it return `errHijackAlreadyWritten`. It now rejects only when `w.size > 0`.\n\nI added a \"hijack after header write should succeed\" case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` in `response_writer_test.go`. **GATE PASS:** the new case fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\nI only ran the `TestResponseWriterHijack*` tests, not the full suite, and I didn't test against a real websocket library."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1150,"cache_read_input_tokens":34107,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1150,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9377cc51-d429-428f-a1db-118e70c5b7a3","uuid":"a4a47437-bb30-4dd2-9fa2-84e73870abdc","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:33:42.569Z","request_id":"req_011CgAG8WSNvHai5CJNXLgf3"}
